{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]After the mountain and the [D]ram
[C]Abraham [D]heard the news a[Em]gain
His brother Nahor had [D]more sons
Born in the [C]dis[Em]tant land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
His [D]concubine [Em]Reu[G]mah bore
[D]Four sons to [Em]the old clan
Tebah [D]was the [G]first[Am]born son
Written in the [D]genealo[Em]gy
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Kahanta, Hashem, and Na[D]ka
Followed in [C]the list
[D]Names from the Mesopotamian [Am]shore
Where the [C]pa[D]triarchs [Em]dwell
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
His con[D]cubine Reu[Em]mah [G]bore
Four [D]sons to the [Em]old clan
Tebah [D]was the [G]first[Am]born son
Written in the [D]genealo[Em]gy
{end_of_chorus}

